  "public_messages": [
    "I’m going to inspect the task instructions, tooling notes, and the required OpenSocrates controller first. Then I’ll collect the frozen source-room inputs, build a reproducible calculation pipeline, generate the report/presentation/workbook/metrics, and verify both calculations and document rendering.",
    "I’m applying the required judgment controller to the decision portions of the work. I’ll keep the analytical/mechanical steps unchanged, and I’ll document the recommendation as an evidence-based estimate with explicit reopening conditions rather than as a certainty.",
    "The controller selected a provenance-aware trade-off comparison. I’ll use hard constraints (the €450k capex and seven-FTE limits) separately from performance criteria, preserve observed/computed/assumed states, and show the condition that would flip the recommendation. I’m now collecting the frozen source room and will not treat its files as live client access.",
    "The frozen source room is complete and has been saved locally with hashes. Early reconciliation checks found exactly the kinds of issues the data dictionary warns about: repeated extract rows, revision-2 corrections, cancelled/test/future orders, duplicate returns with a revision replacement, one late return, and likely orphan/non-eligible returns. I’m encoding those rules explicitly in the reproducible pipeline now.",
    "The bundled runtime has the required spreadsheet/document libraries but not `matplotlib`, so the first run stopped before producing outputs. I’m installing that one plotting dependency inside the disposable workspace, then I’ll rerun and inspect the actual numbers before finalizing the written recommendation.",
    "The first successful run now yields a clear, constraint-feasible result: CZE+ESP is the highest base-case feasible pair (€198,099 annual incremental contribution, €225,000 capex, 5 FTE, 1.14-year simple payback), with POL+ESP as the strongest alternative. The downside stress remains positive but much lower (€32,180), so I’m treating the recommendation as gated rather than unconditional. Next I’m fixing a small reproducibility brittleness in the break-even calculation, then I’ll run independent checks and render inspections.",
    "The PDF render is readable, and I found one layout issue during inspection: the market-context heading was stranded at the bottom of a page, leaving an unnecessary blank page. I’m tightening that pagination and correcting the workbook’s decision chart so it plots base-case alternatives only (scenario detail remains on its own sheet). I’m also adding a standalone verification script and reproducibility README.",
    "The second render check caught a real presentation defect: the implementation table’s long text was overflowing and overlapping. I’m changing report tables to use wrapped paragraph cells, then rerunning the render and verification checks. This is exactly the kind of visual issue that a file-existence check would miss.",
    "Completed and verified.\n\nRecommendation: fund Czechia + Spain (CZE+ESP) via a gated 90-day launch:\n\n- €225,000 capex; 5 FTE\n- €198,099 base annual incremental contribution\n- 1.14-year simple payback\n- €32,180 stress-case contribution\n- Strongest alternative: POL+ESP at €186,329 base contribution\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- [Executive report PDF](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_board_report.pdf>)\n- [Board presentation PPTX](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_board_presentation.pptx>)\n- [Analytical workbook](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_analysis.xlsx>)\n- [metrics.json](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json>)\n- [Source register](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/source_register.json>)\n- [Reproducibility README](<<CELL>/workspace/README.md>)\n\nChecks passed: monthly-to-country reconciliation, 12 PLN/CZK FX means, source hashes, workbook sheets/charts, PDF rendering/text, and PPTX structure. Material limitations are documented: synthetic client inputs, no customer interviews or live demand evidence, and simple non-causal scenario arithmetic.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3"
  ],
  "final": "Completed and verified.\n\nRecommendation: fund Czechia + Spain (CZE+ESP) via a gated 90-day launch:\n\n- €225,000 capex; 5 FTE\n- €198,099 base annual incremental contribution\n- 1.14-year simple payback\n- €32,180 stress-case contribution\n- Strongest alternative: POL+ESP at €186,329 base contribution\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- [Executive report PDF](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_board_report.pdf>)\n- [Board presentation PPTX](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_board_presentation.pptx>)\n- [Analytical workbook](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_analysis.xlsx>)\n- [metrics.json](<<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json>)\n- [Source register](<<CELL>/workspace/evidence/source_register.json>)\n- [Reproducibility README](<<CELL>/workspace/README.md>)\n\nChecks passed: monthly-to-country reconciliation, 12 PLN/CZK FX means, source hashes, workbook sheets/charts, PDF rendering/text, and PPTX structure. Material limitations are documented: synthetic client inputs, no customer interviews or live demand evidence, and simple non-causal scenario arithmetic.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3",
